SUBJECTIVE

Chief Complaint: "Every joint in my hands and knees is screaming, I have a burning rash across my face, and there is a sharp, stabbing pain in my ribs when I take a deep breath."
History of Present Illness: Patient presents with an acute, severe multi-system inflammatory crisis. Timeline: Insidious onset of profound, debilitating systemic fatigue over the past month, completely out of proportion to exertion. Over the last 48 hours, following significant sunlight exposure, the patient developed a severe flare of symmetrical polyarthritis predominantly affecting the small joints of the hands, wrists, and knees. Concurrently, a classic, burning erythematous malar butterfly rash erupted across the cheeks and nasal bridge. Most concerning, the patient reports a 12-hour history of pleuritic chest pain—a sharp shortness of breath and stabbing pain directly tied to active, deep inspiration. Reports a recurrent low-grade fever.
Functional Status: Acutely bedbound; completely immobilized by severe polyarthritis and profound systemic exhaustion.
Social/Safety Concerns: High risk of developing severe cardiopulmonary complications (pericardial effusion) if the autoimmune cascade is not rapidly halted.

OBJECTIVE

Vitals: BP: 118/76 | HR: 110 | Temp: 37.8 | RR: 20 (Shallow) | SpO2: 98% | Wt: 65 Kg
General: Alert, looking profoundly systemically unwell, taking shallow breaths, with a visible, striking facial rash.
Physical Exam: Skin reveals a classic, raised, erythematous malar butterfly rash strictly sparing the nasolabial folds. Musculoskeletal exam demonstrates severe, symmetrical, non-erosive polyarthritis in the MCPs, PIPs, wrists, and knees. Joints are exquisitely tender but lack the massive, boggy, destructive synovial effusions typical of severe RA. Cardiovascular exam reveals a regular tachycardia; no distinct pericardial friction rub is auscultated currently, but heart sounds are normal. Respiratory exam shows clear lung fields bilaterally, but marked pain guarding and splinting on deep inspiration, highly consistent with acute pleuritis. Oral cavity reveals a painless mucosal ulcer on the hard palate.
